{
  "id": "Compound::DB01174 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Phenobarbital is implicated in the metabolic activation of multiple substrates through its interaction with Cyp2c18, which is a key enzyme in the metabolic pathway of Diclofenac and Arachidonic Acid. The evidence suggests that Phenobarbital binds to Cyp2c18, leading to its participation in the metabolic processes of these substrates. This binding and participation are linked to the activation of Cyp2b6, which is part of the metabolic pathway for these substrates. The integration of these pathways indicates that Phenobarbital may influence Cyp2b6 through its role in modulating the activity of Cyp2c18, thereby affecting the metabolic capacity of Cyp2b6. The relationship between Phenobarbital and Cyp2b6 is thus mediated through the enzyme Cyp2c18, highlighting a complex interplay in the metabolic processes involving these entities.",
